# Cloudflare Pages caching rules.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.  `stamp_build.py` derives a cache-buster from the DATA
# and appends it to every JSON fetch as `?v=<BUILD>`, so a rebuilt corpus can
# never be served stale.  But the HTML that CONTAINS that stamp is fetched at a
# plain URL with no version on it — so a returning browser can hold yesterday's
# reader, complete with yesterday's BUILD, and go on requesting yesterday's
# data quite correctly.  Fixes made in `reader2.html` or `search.html` reach
# nobody until the page itself revalidates.
#
# So: HTML always revalidates (it is small), and the versioned data is
# immutable (it is large, and its URL changes whenever it does).

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
